That's Tosei, so it doesn't help that Tosei also made all these games, too.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:27.180
So, when we're talking about Ninja Kid, the first thing was like, oh, is this going to

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.060
be like the rest of them?

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.420
But I think that this game is not like the rest of those.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.260
And I actually had a really good time with this one, even right from the get-go, because

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.000
it was more like Super Mario Bros.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.500
I really appreciated that overworld map, which Super Mario Bros.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.680
didn't even have yet. I mean, that's like a Super Mario Bros.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:49.260
3 thing. And I think also the scrolling mechanic, you know, it's an infinite scroller.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.600
You just keep going left to right.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:56.320
But there is kind of like a spatial awareness of, like, where you are on that map.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.700
You know, you kind of see where the loop is and stuff like that.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.780
So, I thought that was, like, nice to be able to go back and forth.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.800
If you saw an enemy that you might have missed, you could run back real fast and they might

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.000
still be there, provided you haven't, like, ran too far off.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.580
Yeah. So, I appreciated this game on just, like, its fundamentals.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.700
But maybe now, you know, like, we should talk about the objective and then, you know,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:22.140
probably we're going to get into the flaws of the game pretty quickly after we talk about

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:28.780
that. Oh, yeah. So, the objective for Ninja Kid, it's, like, it's kind of weird because there's not really

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.300
a lot of story given to you, but you're the Ninja Kid.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:38.040
Uh-huh. And you have to, like, hit up these temples across the overworld map where different things

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:43.840
will happen. It'll be, like, guerrilla warfare or dogfight or Inferno.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:49.540
Yeah. It's, like, I don't know what those things mean and the objectives are pretty unclear,

